  "headline": "MPR Schedules Vice President Election For December 10 And 11, 2026",
  "seoTitle": "MPR Discusses Vice President Election Date",
  "metaDescription": "The MPR has proposed holding the plenary session to elect a new Vice President of Indonesia on December 10 and 11, 2026, following recent resignations.",
  "aiSummaryBullets": [
    "The MPR Ad Hoc Committee proposed a two-day plenary session on December 10 and 11, 2026, to select a successor for the vacant Vice Presidency.",
    "Verification teams are currently vetting two vice-presidential candidates by coordinating with the KPK, Supreme Court, Police, and Ministry of Finance.",
    "The MPR has finalized six draft decrees to facilitate the legal process of filling the vice-presidential vacancy after the previous official stepped down."
  ],
  "aiContextParagraph": "The Indonesian People's Consultative Assembly (MPR) has initiated formal procedures to fill the Vice President's office, which has remained vacant since Gibran Rakabuming Raka resigned on November 12, 2026. The MPR's Ad Hoc Committee is currently overseeing the selection process, which includes the vetting of two proposed candidates. Verification teams have engaged with several state institutions, including the Corruption Eradication Commission (KPK), the Supreme Court, the National Police, and the Ministry of Finance, to ensure the candidates have no criminal records or tax arrears. The Assembly has also prepared six specific decrees to guide the election proceedings. A plenary session to finalize the selection has been proposed for December 10 and 11, 2026, following the conclusion of the verification work conducted by the assembly's working groups.",
